          Updating CNet Amiga BackUp, v3.00/3.01/3.50 to v3.51!
-=-=-=-=-=-=-=-=-=-=-=-=-=-=-=-=-=-=-=-=-=-=-=-=-=-=-=-=-=-=-=-=-=-=-=-=-=-=-

    If this is your FIRST time using CNet Amiga BackUp, then please refer to
the "CNetBackUp.README!" file right now.

    If you're presently using v3.50 of CNet Amiga BackUp, then follow these
steps to upgrade to v3.51: (If using v3.00 or v3.01, skip below...)

1. Replace ALL command files with the NEW ones included in this archive.

2. Run the included "CNetBackUp_UPDATE351" script from within your designated
   "CNetAmigaBackUp/" path using one of those RUNA commands, or else you can
   temporarily add it as a pfile. This update will make sure none of your
   existing backup files is using the ".BAK" extension. If so, you'll be
   asked to specify a different extension for that BackUp set. All proper
   changes will be made to your config files, and any existing archive files,
   logs, etc. will be renamed using the new extension you designate.

3. Be sure to read the HISTORY and README files for important informtion on
   the CHANGES and ADDITIONS made to this version, notably CLONE BackUps!

4. That's It!

    If you're presently using v3.00, or v3.01 of CNet Amiga BackUp, follow
these steps to upgrade to this NEW version:

1. Replace ALL command files with the NEW ones included in this archive.

2. Run the included "CNetBackUp_UPDATE" script from within your designated
   "CNetAmigaBackUp/" path using one of those RUNA commands, or else you can
   temporarily add it as a pfile. This update will make some additions to
   your "CNetBackUp.CFG" file, to which you can further modify later.

3. Be sure to read the HISTORY and README files for important informtion on
   the CHANGES and ADDITIONS made to this version!

4. That's It!

